  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal, by reason of the loss of soft landscaping, the installation of additional hardstanding, inadequate information regarding boundary treatments and drainage, and its impact on the existing street tree, would harm the character and appearance of the host property, the street scene and the wider area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies CC1, CC2 and SC7 of the Local Plan and the Residential Extensions Guidelines.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, by reason of the provision of a second vehicular crossover to a property that already benefits from an existing vehicular access, its location within the minimum required distance of a road junction, the absence of details regarding the treatment and operation of the existing pedestrian access, the lack of an appropriate boundary treatment to prevent vehicles crossing other sections of the frontage to the detriment of pedestrian safety, and the adverse impact on an existing street tree located within the required visibility splays, would be detrimental to highway and pedestrian safety. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy EC2 of the Local Plan and the Council's Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking Policy (2016)."
  ],
